            <ArticleTitle>Coronary artery pseudoaneurysm following blunt trauma.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>563-5</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1111/j.1540-8191.2012.01474.x</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A 42-year-old male was admitted with persistent atypical chest pain following a motorcycle accident six months previously. A pseudoaneurysm, diagnosed by transthoracic echocardiography and computed tomography, was excised and the right coronary artery underwent bypass grafting.</AbstractText>
